9.17, 12.83, 12.31} for Q_max = {1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64}; R(Bern, minor) ≈ 10.7 ± 0.6 across all Q_max. Z-scores progress {214, 80, 114, 53, 11, 3.1, 3.1}σ — primes converge to Bernoulli noise floor as Q_max → ∞, with persistent ~3σ residual reflecting cumulative O(Q²) HL peaks at q > Q_max. Scaling rule R(prime, minor; Q_max) ≈ √π(N) / φ(q*) where q* = smallest squarefree integer > Q_max verified to ~10% across all (N, Q_max) cells. **Mechanism for closure mode I (partial closure with HL fingerprint as new content)**: the L^∞ structure decomposes EXACTLY into the Hardy-Littlewood circle-method singular series. Major-arc R(a/q) = √π(N)·μ²(q)/φ(q) is the exponential-sum identity Σ_{p≤N} e^{2πi p a/q} ≈ μ(q)/φ(q)·π(N) (classical Vinogradov / Hardy-Littlewood); the bare ‖f‖_∞ is dominated by q=2 parity. **Erdős-extremal flatness DECISIVELY REFUTED**: R_N → ∞ as √π(N), the OPPOSITE extreme; primes are one of the LEAST flat 0/1 supports possible (saturating the trivial upper bound from above via parity). **Distinct from**: D10/E2.20 (Mahler = log integral, geometric mean) — D27 makes the parity major-arc contribution to the Jensen integral explicit at z=-1; D25 (Stein-Tomas L^p, finite p) — D27 covers the p=∞ endpoint; CLOSED_PATHS line 778/E7.16 (Friedman/Ramanujan prime-Cayley spectral gap) — that uses the prime SET as Cayley generators on Z/NZ, this uses χ_P as polynomial coefficients. **Adds EDGE E2.21**: R(a/q; primes) = √π(N)·μ²(q)/φ(q) + O(√log N) at every rational; ‖f_N‖_∞ = (1+o(1))√π(N) attained at z=-1; provides the L^∞-norm endpoint of the L^p Fourier-side category. **Negative-shape consequence**: any L^∞-Chebyshev-style compression of f_N cannot beat √π(N) storage — parity peak forces this lower bound; rules out "flat-polynomial" representation of χ_P as polylog primality witness. **Cross-domain ingredient (Newman / Erdős / Littlewood / Bourgain Λ(p) extremal-polynomial L^∞ harmonic analysis) performed real work**: first project quantitative use; CROSS_DOMAI