    358	### A7 — Geometric Complexity Theory (GCT) obstruction for formula complexity of χ_P
    359	
    360	**Question:** Encode `χ_P^{(n)} : \{1, ..., 2^n\} → \{0, 1\}` as a
    361	multi-affine polynomial `f_χ_P^{(n)}(x_1, ..., x_n) = Σ_{S ⊆ [n], \mathrm{val}(S) \in \mathrm{PRIMES}} ∏_{i \in S} x_i`
    362	where `\mathrm{val}(S) := Σ_{i \in S} 2^{i-1}`. The Mulmuley-Sohoni 2001
    363	GCT program seeks formula / determinant lower bounds on a polynomial
    364	`f` via *orbit closure containment* in `\mathrm{End}(V) \cdot f` and
    365	*occurrence obstructions* — irreducible `GL(V)`-representations
    366	appearing in the coordinate ring `\mathbb{C}[\overline{GL_n \cdot f}]`
    367	but NOT in the determinant orbit closure. Question: identify a
    368	representation-theoretic GCT obstruction proving `f_χ_P^{(n)}` has
    369	formula size super-polynomial in `n` (equivalently, χ_P ∉ NC^1
    370	unconditionally), OR identify a GCT-style obstruction to TC^0
    371	computability that does not reduce to AKS-family closures (E5.3,
    372	E7.10) or to Brandt-style diagonalisation (E5.8).
    373	
    374	**Why frontier:** the project's TC^0 attacks have run via SAT search
    375	(A1, partial closure S84 — empty at depth ≤ 5 size ≤ 2000 for `n=8`)
    376	and proof-complexity / bounded arithmetic (A4 PROPOSED). GCT is
    377	**representation-theoretic algebraic geometry** — fundamentally
    378	different machinery, never used in the project. Bürgisser-Ikenmeyer
    379	2017 *FOCS* "no occurrence obstruction" theorem proved that the
